{
  "id": "InvIntakeMain0001",
  "name": "Invoice intake with human approval (Claude + MCP)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Invoice intake with human approval\nEmail (IMAP) or webhook -> PDF -> MCP server `extract_invoice` (Claude + rule checks) -> if every check passes, DM the approver in Slack and wait -> approve or reject via MCP.\n\n**Nothing is filed until a person clicks Approve.** Failed checks go to a review channel instead.\n\nSet up: fill in the **Config** node; create two *Header Auth* credentials (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`): **Invoice MCP (read)** with a READ token and **Invoice MCP (approver)** with an APPROVER token. Pick them in the HTTP nodes after import. Error workflow: import `error-alert.json` too.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 5
      },
      "name": "Note: what this does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        -480
      ],
      "id": "06de3ca7-0b2f-5341-8258-c78c8515f35f"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Two tokens, two scopes.** The extract call uses a read-scope token, so even a bug in this half of the flow can't approve anything. Only the two decision nodes hold the approver token, and they only run after a Slack click.\n\n**Retries:** every MCP call retries 3x, 5 s apart. If extract still fails, the red error output posts an alert; anything else that fails triggers the Error workflow.\n\n**Client data:** successful executions are not saved (Settings), so invoice contents don't pile up in n8n's database.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 3
      },
      "name": "Note: least privilege",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        430
      ],
      "id": "620c90fe-a92c-5e5d-baf0-60a4354e2ad5"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mailbox": "INBOX",
        "postProcessAction": "read",
        "downloadAttachments": true,
        "format": "resolved",
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "New invoice email (IMAP)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailReadImap",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2860,
        0
      ],
      "id": "00e453db-bab6-5155-9ad5-c9b02ca94023"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "invoice-intake",
        "authentication": "headerAuth",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {
          "binaryPropertyName": "data"
        }
      },
      "name": "Invoice upload (webhook)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "1cbabc6e-3861-5c16-93bb-e7f96c60a298"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Turn each PDF attachment (email) or uploaded file (webhook) into base64 for the MCP call.\n// Non-PDF attachments are ignored. Nothing is logged here.\nconst out = [];\nconst items = $input.all();\nfor (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n  const bin = items[i].binary || {};\n  for (const key of Object.keys(bin)) {\n    const meta = bin[key];\n    const isPdf = (meta.mimeType || '').includes('pdf') || (meta.fileName || '').toLowerCase().endsWith('.pdf');\n    if (!isPdf) continue;\n    const buf = await this.helpers.getBinaryDataBuffer(i, key);\n    out.push({ json: { pdf_base64: buf.toString('base64'), source_name: meta.fileName || 'upload.pdf' } });\n  }\n}\nreturn out;"
      },
      "name": "Pick PDF attachments",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        260,
        0
      ],
      "id": "69330a35-7083-56c3-9d00-ef143a154a8a"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "cfg-url",
              "name": "mcp_url",
              "value": "http://invoice-mcp:8787/mcp",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "cfg-appr",
              "name": "approver_name",
              "value": "aishu",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "cfg-slack",
              "name": "approver_slack_id",
              "value": "U0000000000",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "cfg-rev",
              "name": "review_channel",
              "value": "#ap-review",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        520,
        0
      ],
      "id": "65626d30-ffe6-5648-8805-5789a4a42e65"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Config').item.json.mcp_url }}",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Accept",
              "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: '2.0', id: $execution.id, method: 'tools/call', params: { name: 'extract_invoice', arguments: { pdf_base64: $json.pdf_base64, source_name: $json.source_name } } }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 180000
        }
      },
      "name": "Extract invoice (MCP, read token)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        780,
        0
      ],
      "id": "afdf5580-2fba-5c00-b977-b719a26504a8",
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "Invoice MCP (read)"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Unwrap the JSON-RPC reply from the MCP server. A tool error (e.g. Claude declined,\n// or the reply was cut off) is thrown on purpose so the Error workflow alerts a person.\nconst r = $json;\nif (r.error) throw new Error('MCP error: ' + r.error.message);\nif (!r.result) throw new Error('MCP reply had no result');\nif (r.result.isError) throw new Error('extract_invoice failed: ' + (r.result.content?.[0]?.text || 'unknown'));\nconst s = r.result.structuredContent ?? JSON.parse(r.result.content[0].text);\nconst f = s.fields;\nreturn { json: {\n  id: s.id,\n  all_checks_passed: s.all_checks_passed,\n  failed_checks: s.failed_checks,\n  label: s.label,\n  cost_usd: s.cost_usd,\n  vendor: f.vendor_name,\n  invoice_number: f.invoice_number,\n  document_type: f.document_type,\n  total: f.total,\n  currency: f.currency,\n  due_date: f.due_date,\n  po_number: f.po_number,\n  // \"Drafts cite their sources\": the approval message shows where each key value was read.\n  sources: (f.sources || []).map(x => `${x.field}: p.${x.page} \"${x.quote}\"`).join('\\n'),\n} };"
      },
      "name": "Read MCP result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1040,
        -100
      ],
      "id": "a1373b5f-dcf0-5d1b-be3f-44092e9c4750"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "3c88e2eb-32ca-5b2d-9ec5-f84b2bfe5644",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.all_checks_passed === true }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "All checks passed?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1300,
        0
      ],
      "id": "f912f9d2-74cd-5176-aaa9-df320c8edc3b"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "sendAndWait",
        "select": "user",
        "user": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Config').item.json.approver_slack_id }}"
        },
        "message": "={{ '*Invoice needs your approval*\\n' + $json.vendor + ' ' + $json.invoice_number + ' (' + $json.document_type + ')\\n' + 'Total: ' + $json.currency + ' ' + $json.total + ' | Due: ' + ($json.due_date || 'none') + ' | PO: ' + ($json.po_number || 'none') + '\\n' + 'All checks passed.\\n\\nSources:\\n' + $json.sources + '\\n\\n' + $json.label + (($json.cost_usd !== null) ? ' | extraction cost $' + $json.cost_usd.toFixed(4) : '') + '\\nRecord: ' + $json.id }}",
        "responseType": "approval",
        "approvalOptions": {
          "values": {
            "approvalType": "double",
            "approveLabel": "Approve and file",
            "disapproveLabel": "Reject"
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "limitWaitTime": {
            "values": {
              "limitType": "afterTimeInterval",
              "resumeAmount": 3,
              "resumeUnit": "days"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "name": "Ask approver in Slack (wait)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        1560,
        -100
      ],
      "id": "d289d512-953a-543d-9ceb-f1a97280941d"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
